    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Brice Turang** (75.06) and **Corbin Carroll** (81.86) anchor the lineup as our most potent assets. **Brice Turang** earns a top-tier score thanks to a favorable matchup against Bubba Chandler; the projection models explicitly bake in a +4% efficiency boost due to Chandler\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an prime environment for **Brice Turang** to hunt for stolen bases. **Corbin Carroll** remains an auto-start despite facing Michael King; while King is a formidable arm, the combination of a high-leadoff spot and the stolen base upside against a pitcher with an average hold rate keeps **Corbin Carroll** in the elite tier. Both **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes** are strong starts today, benefiting from high-leadoff spots and SP skill metrics that favor their profiles against Michael King and Shane Bieber, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the periphery was the utilization of **Jose Caballero** (57.32) versus our depth. While **Jose Caballero** sits on the cusp of the \"Strong\" rating, he is held in the lineup primarily for his capacity to contribute to our scarcity-heavy SB target. He narrowly edges out potential depth pieces like **Zach McKinstry** or **Travis Bazzana** because his high-volume sprint speed remains a priority over marginal batting average gains. We are exercising caution with **Dalton Rushing** (40.07), whose score is suppressed by a negative L/L platoon disadvantage against Matthew Boyd and a deep-order placement; he remains a marginal start strictly due to his positional necessity. We are closely monitoring the lineup postings for **Seiya Suzuki** and **James Wood**, both of whom are projected as \"Strong\" plays; **James Wood** specifically warrants attention given his elite .422 xwOBA, which suggests he could outperform his score if he navigates the tough matchup against Aaron Nola. Note that **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Austin Riley** are currently sidelined or inactive, further limiting our rotational flexibility.",
